    "author": "William Shakespeare",
    "description": "Hamlet is Shakespeare's most popular, and most puzzling, play. It follows the form of a \u0393\u00c7\u00a3revenge tragedy,\u0393\u00c7\u00a5 in which the hero, Hamlet, seeks vengeance against his father\u0393\u00c7\u00d6s murderer, his uncle Claudius, now the king of Denmark. Much of its fascination, however, lies in its uncertainties. Among them: What is the Ghost\u0393\u00c7\u00f6Hamlet's father demanding justice, a tempting demon, an angelic messenger? Does Hamlet go mad, or merely pretend to? Once he is sure that Claudius is a murderer, why does he not act? Was his mother, Gertrude, unfaithful to her husband or complicit in his murder? The authoritative edition of Hamlet from The Folger Shakespeare Library, the trusted and widely used Shakespeare series for students and general readers, is now available as an eBook. Features include: \u252c\u2556 The exact text of the printed book for easy cross-reference \u252c\u2556 Hundreds of hypertext links for instant navigation \u252c\u2556 Freshly edited text based on the best early printed version of the play \u252c\u2556 Full explanatory notes conveniently placed on pages facing the text of the play \u252c\u2556 Scene-by-scene plot summaries \u252c\u2556 A key to famous lines and phrases \u252c\u2556 An introduction to reading Shakespeare\u0393\u00c7\u00d6s language \u252c\u2556 Illustrations from the Folger Shakespeare Library\u0393\u00c7\u00d6s vast holdings of rare books \u252c\u2556 An essay by a leading Shakespeare scholar providing a modern perspective on the play",
