    "description": "The colorful staff of a hedonistic club attends to the unconventional and sometimes humorous needs of their members while navigating their own friendships, rivalries and romances in this contemporary series. An actor for the California collective, Black is one of several personnel using a pseudonym. He embarks on recruiting Becky Martin with the ultimate intention of bringing her onto the staff, not as his subordinate, but as his equal. Plagued by a recurring nightmare and stagnant life, Becky actively entertains his proposal. Black\u0393\u00c7\u00d6s closest ally is Cade, the in-house lawyer looking to fill the void of having no genuine connection since coming on board. He sets his sights on an ambitious target after years of being rejected by his first choice, the showy Hannah Sedgwick. Along with Cade, Hannah has made her home on Black\u0393\u00c7\u00d6s so-called side of the fence. Certain staff find solidarity in Black\u0393\u00c7\u00d6s laidback reticence while others are drawn to the unwavering control imposed by Random, the resident doctor and head of the collective. Random\u0393\u00c7\u00d6s most stanch ally is Reno, a snarky, attractive hacker and master of improvisation. Also in his camp are Shay Fontaine and Trip, the two most recently hired Tops. Shay fills the member relations role and has a get-it-done work ethic that Random regards. Trip is another actor, whose private issue brewing back home in Oklahoma will challenge his capacity while also ushering a breath of fresh air into his life. Volume 1 brings Black and Random\u0393\u00c7\u00d6s sides together in the equally personal and work-oriented goal of recruiting Becky Martin, who becomes the mutual mission of these two Dominants, binding them over the course of time. It\u0393\u00c7\u00d6s never too dark and never too light in this forward-moving series of desires, mind games, debauchery and the option to live an offbeat life: The Alternative.",
